@parties
go-to: menu

<span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span> - *Partido Socialista Obrero Español* (Spanish Socialist Workers' Party) - this is us. We are a socialist and democratic party of the working class, founded in 1879 and closely tied to the <span style="color: #700000;">**UGT**</span> trade union. We are among the foremost defenders of the Republic we helped found in 1931.

<span style="color: #4a7d3a;">**Republican Left**</span> - *Izquierda Republicana* - Manuel Azaña's party of the progressive, secular, republican middle class - lawyers, teachers, and professionals. Anti-clerical and reformist rather than socialist, they are our closest and most natural ally, and our senior partner in the Republican-Socialist coalition and later the Popular Front.

Current relations: [+ izq_rep_relation : relationships +]

<span style="color: #d9a441;">**Radical Party**</span> - *Partido Republicano Radical* - Alejandro Lerroux's party, nominally republican and once anti-clerical, but increasingly a vehicle for pragmatic office-holding and conservative accommodation. Governed with us in 1931-33, then swung right into coalition with the <span style="color: #003755;">**CEDA**</span>.

Current relations: [+ radical_relation : relationships +]

<span style="color: #003755;">**CEDA**</span> - *Confederación Española de Derechas Autónomas* (Spanish Confederation of the Autonomous Right) - Gil-Robles's mass Catholic-authoritarian party, formed in 1933 from Catholic and agrarian groups. Ambiguous about the Republic itself, it draws on smallholders, devout Catholics, and landowners, and its youth movement openly admires Italian and German fascism.

Current relations: [+ ceda_relation : relationships +]

<span style="color: #700000;">**PCE**</span> - *Partido Comunista de España* (Communist Party of Spain) - a small Marxist-Leninist party following the Comintern line, historically hostile to us as rivals for the workers' loyalty, but increasingly open to a common front against the authoritarian right as the decade wears on.

Current relations: [+ pce_relation : relationships +]

**Monarchists** - Renovación Española and the Carlists (*Comunión Tradicionalista*) - two rival currents of the anti-Republican right, one favoring the exiled Alfonso XIII, the other a rival Carlist pretender, united mainly by hostility to the Republic itself and, increasingly, by conspiracy with sympathetic army officers.

Current relations: [+ monarchist_relation : relationships +]

<span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Falange**</span> - *Falange Española* - José Antonio Primo de Rivera's small fascist movement, fusing nationalism, corporatism, and paramilitary violence. Electorally negligible so far, but its street violence and appeal to junior officers make it a growing threat.

Current relations: [+ falange_relation : relationships +]

**Others** - a scattering of small parties and regionalist forces: Catalan (<span style="color: #FFB612;">**ERC**</span>, the Lliga), Basque (<span style="color: #EE2D24;">**PNV**</span>), and Galician nationalists, along with minor agrarian and monarchist splinters. The anarcho-syndicalist <span style="color: #333333;">**CNT**</span>-<span style="color: #333333;">**FAI**</span>, though it does not contest elections, commands the loyalty of a large share of the industrial and landless working class and can swing an election through participation or abstention alone.

@paramilitaries
on-arrival: {!
Q.ugt_militia_strength = Math.round(Q.ugt_militia_strength);
Q.requetes_strength = Math.round(Q.requetes_strength);
Q.falange_militia_strength = Math.round(Q.falange_militia_strength);
Q.cnt_militia_strength = Math.round(Q.cnt_militia_strength);
!}
go-to: menu

**Paramilitary groups:**

**UGT/PSOE militia**: affiliated with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span> and the socialist trade union UGT. Historically, this has been a largely unarmed organization, though it arms itself as the crisis deepens.

Strength: [+ ugt_militia_strength +] thousand

Militarization: [+ ugt_militia_militancy : militancy +]

**CNT-FAI militia**: the armed wing of the anarcho-syndicalist movement, independent of and often hostile to the <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span>.

Strength: [+ cnt_militia_strength +] thousand

Militarization: [+ cnt_militia_militancy : militancy +]

**Requetés**: the Carlist monarchist militia, a right-wing paramilitary organization associated with the <span style="color: #2E3B6E;">**Monarchists**</span>.

Strength: [+ requetes_strength +] thousand

Militarization: [+ requetes_militancy : militancy +]

**Falange militia**: the paramilitary wing of the <span style="color: #14322a;">**Falange**</span>.

Strength: [+ falange_militia_strength +] thousand

Militarization: [+ falange_militia_militancy : militancy +]

**Official military/paramilitary groups:**

**Spanish Army**: [+ army_strength +] thousand troops.

Loyalty: [+ army_loyalty : loyalty +]

**Guardia Civil**: [+ guardia_civil_strength +] thousand members. A conservative rural gendarmerie of uncertain loyalty to the Republic.

Loyalty: [+ guardia_civil_loyalty : loyalty +]

**Guardia de Asalto**: [+ asalto_strength +] thousand members. An urban police force created by the Republic specifically to be loyal to it.

Loyalty: [+ asalto_loyalty : loyalty +]



@factions

**Internal factions of the** <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span>

Overall dissent: [+ dissent_percent : dissent +]

**Caballeristas (Left)**

Followers of Francisco Largo Caballero, the "Spanish Lenin." Many favor closer cooperation with the <span style="color: #700000;">**PCE**</span> and the anarcho-syndicalist unions, and some support extra-parliamentary action to defend the working class.

Strength: [+ left_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ left_dissent : dissent +]

**Besteiristas (Centrists)**

Followers of Julián Besteiro's orthodox <span style="color: #9B0000;">Marxism</span>. They seek a middle course between reform and revolution, while defending the democratic state and rejecting collaboration with the bourgeois parties.

Strength: [+ center_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ center_dissent : dissent +]

**UGT (Labor)**

Members of the <span style="color: #700000;">**UGT**</span>, the socialist trade union federation. Their goal is economic reform and material benefits for organized workers.

Strength: [+ labor_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ labor_dissent : dissent +]

**Prietistas (Reformists)**

Followers of Indalecio Prieto. They are pragmatic participants in government, and seek to expand the welfare state and defend the Republic against both the authoritarian right and the revolutionary left. [? if psoe_catalonia : They are dominant in the Catalan government. ?]

Strength: [+ reformist_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ reformist_dissent : dissent +]

[? if neorevisionism: **Anti-Fascist Mobilization** ?]

[? if neorevisionism: This current focuses on defending the Republic against the authoritarian right, while also expanding the party's base beyond organized labor to build a broader popular movement. They support new propaganda methods and extra-parliamentary mobilization in defense of the Republic. ?]

[? if neorevisionism: Strength: [+ neorevisionist_strength : strength +] ?]

[? if neorevisionism: Dissent: [+ neorevisionist_dissent : dissent +] ?]

[? if social_patriot: **National Unity Current** ?]

[? if social_patriot: A small tendency that argues the <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">**UGT**</span> should set aside class conflict in the name of national unity above party or class. Other factions view their positions as unprincipled accommodation with the existing order. ?]

[? if social_patriot: Strength: [+ social_patriot_strength : strength +] ?]

[? if social_patriot: Dissent: [+ social_patriot_dissent : dissent +] ?]

@figures
title: Figures and Charts
go-to: menu
on-display: {!
const data = [];

if (Q.psoe_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "psoe",
        "legend": "PSOE",
        "name": "PSOE",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.psoe_r * Q.cortes_size),
    });
}

if (Q.pce_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "pce",
        "legend": "PCE",
        "name": "PCE",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.pce_r * Q.cortes_size),
    });
}

if (Q.ceda_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "ceda",
        "legend": "CEDA",
        "name": "CEDA",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.ceda_r * Q.cortes_size),
    });
}

if (Q.izq_rep_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "izq_rep",
        "legend": "IR",
        "name": "IR",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.izq_rep_r * Q.cortes_size),
    });
}

if (Q.radical_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "radical",
        "legend": "PRR",
        "name": "PRR",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.radical_r * Q.cortes_size),
    });
}

if (Q.monarchist_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "monarchist",
        "legend": "Mon.",
        "name": "Monarchist",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.monarchist_r * Q.cortes_size),
    });
}

if (Q.falange_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "falange",
        "legend": "FE",
        "name": "Falange",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.falange_r * Q.cortes_size),
    });
}

if (Q.other_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "other",
        "legend": "Other",
        "name": "Other",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.other_r * Q.cortes_size),
    });
}

if (d3 && window) {
    // get screen width
    var width = 500;
    var height = 500;
    var screenWidth = document.getElementById('content').offsetWidth;
    if (screenWidth < width - 50) {
        width = screenWidth - 50;
        height = width;
        document.getElementById("reichstag").style.height = screenWidth/2 + "px";
    }
    var parliament = d3.parliament();
    parliament.width(width).height(height).innerRadiusCoef(0.4);
    parliament.enter.fromCenter(true).smallToBig(true);
    parliament.exit.toCenter(false).bigToSmall(true);
    d3.select("#reichstag").datum(data).call(parliament);

    var lines = d3.linegraph(false, false,
            Q.parties_graph,
            {'psoe': '#c00000', 'pce': '#8a0303', 'ceda': '#0087DC', 'izq_rep': '#7B2D8E', 'radical': '#E8B23A', 'monarchist': '#2E3B6E', 'falange': '#14322a', 'other': '#888888'},
            {'psoe': 'PSOE', 'pce': 'PCE', 'ceda': 'CEDA', 'izq_rep': 'IR', 'radical': 'PRR', 'monarchist': 'Monarchist', 'falange': 'Falange', 'other': 'Others'});
    lines.width(width).height(400);
    //var svg = lines(Q.election_records);
    if (Q.election_records.length > 0) {
        d3.select("#election_history").datum(Q.election_records).call(lines);
    }
    //document.getElementById('election_history').innerHTML = svg.outerHTML;

    // party support records should not have so many ticks
    if (Q.game_over || (!Q.historical_mode && !Q.rubicon)) {
        var lines_2 = d3.linegraph(true, true,
            Q.parties_graph,
            {'psoe': '#c00000', 'pce': '#8a0303', 'ceda': '#0087DC', 'izq_rep': '#7B2D8E', 'radical': '#E8B23A', 'monarchist': '#2E3B6E', 'falange': '#14322a', 'other': '#888888'},
            {'psoe': 'PSOE', 'pce': 'PCE', 'ceda': 'CEDA', 'izq_rep': 'IR', 'radical': 'PRR', 'monarchist': 'Monarchist', 'falange': 'Falange', 'other': 'Others'});
        lines_2.width(width).height(400);
        d3.select("#party_support_history").datum(Q.party_support_records).call(lines_2);
    }

    // economic stats
    var minInflation = d3.min(Q.economic_records, d => d.inflation);
    var maxUnemployment = d3.max(Q.economic_records, d => d.unemployment);
    var lines_3 = d3.linegraph(true, true, ['inflation', 'unemployment'],
            {'inflation': '#0000FF', 'unemployment': '#FF0000'},
            {'inflation': 'Inflation', 'unemployment': 'Unemployment'},
            maxUnemployment + 5, minInflation - 5, 21);
    lines_3.width(width).height(300);
    d3.select("#economic_history").datum(Q.economic_records).call(lines_3);
}
!}

